A little past nine o'clock, the many morning guests arrived.
It was suddenly very busy in the café.
I stood behind the counter and waited excitedly.
A customer came over to me.
"I would like a cappuccino, please," he said.
It was my very first coffee for a customer.
I started the espresso machine.
Afterwards, I tried to froth the milk.
But I steamed the milk a little too long.
I have not yet learned to control the hot steam completely.
Therefore, it lacked some thick foam on top.
I looked eagerly down into the cup.
Fortunately, it still looked acceptable.
I placed the cup on the counter.
"Here you go," I said with a polite smile.
The customer took his cappuccino.
"Thank you very much," he answered kindly.
He sat down at the first table by the window.
I was very relieved.
I have now fulfilled my first order.
